{% extends "base.html.twig" %}

{% block content %}
  <header class="hero content-measure">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Published records</p>
      <h1>Wordle archive: past answers and hints</h1>
      <p class="lede">Search previous Wordle answers by exact date, puzzle number or five-letter word. Archive links work without JavaScript.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="search-panel card" data-archive-search aria-labelledby="search-heading">
    <h2 id="search-heading">Search the archive</h2>
    <form role="search">
      <label class="field-label" for="archive-query">Date, number or exact word</label>
      <input id="archive-query" type="search" autocomplete="off" placeholder="YYYY-MM-DD, puzzle number or exact word">
      <button type="submit">Search</button>
    </form>
    <p data-search-status aria-live="polite">Showing the current archive.</p>
    <ul class="archive-list" data-search-results></ul>
  </section>

  <nav class="archive-nav" aria-label="Archive years">
    {% for year in years %}<a href="/wordle-answers/{{ year }}/">{{ year }}</a>{% endfor %}
  </nav>

  <section data-default-archive aria-labelledby="archive-heading">
    <h2 id="archive-heading">Newest published records</h2>
    {% include "partials/archive-list.html.twig" %}
  </section>

  {% if total_pages > 1 %}
    <nav class="pagination" aria-label="Archive pages">
      {% for page_number in 1..total_pages %}
        {% if page_number == current_page %}<span aria-current="page">Page {{ page_number }}</span>{% else %}<a href="{% if page_number == 1 %}/wordle-answers/{% else %}/wordle-answers/page/{{ page_number }}/{% endif %}">Page {{ page_number }}</a>{% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </nav>
  {% endif %}

  <section class="section prose" aria-labelledby="archive-guide-heading">
    <h2 id="archive-guide-heading">How to use the Wordle answer archive</h2>
    <p>Enter a date in YYYY-MM-DD format, a public puzzle number or an exact five-letter answer. You can also browse year and month pages when you remember roughly when a puzzle appeared.</p>

    <h2>Find yesterday’s Wordle answer</h2>
    <p>Choose the previous calendar date from the newest published records or search for it directly. Because “yesterday” depends on timezone, every result displays an explicit date and puzzle number.</p>

    <h2>Used Wordle words and repeated answers</h2>
    <p>This archive lists validated published records rather than predicting unused future answers. If the same solution is published on more than one date, each occurrence remains attached to its own date and puzzle number.</p>

    <h2>Wordle archive FAQ</h2>
    <h3>Can I search past Wordle words by answer?</h3>
    <p>Yes. Enter the complete five-letter word. The archive search uses exact matching so a partial word does not reveal unrelated solutions.</p>
    <h3>Does the archive contain every Wordle answer?</h3>
    {% if mode == 'fixture' %}
      <p>It contains only records imported and validated by this project. This private fixture preview is deliberately small and is not presented as a complete historical list.</p>
    {% else %}
      <p>It contains only records imported and validated by this project from the date publication began. It is not presented as a complete historical list.</p>
    {% endif %}
    <h3>Do historical pages change when a new puzzle is published?</h3>
    <p>No. Each dated page stays attached to its original date, while the archive index adds newly validated records.</p>
  </section>
{% endblock %}
